#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Default command: says what lives in this image.
cat <<'EOF'
jakubboucek/pdftools - extracting data from published documents

  pdf-probe <file>                 what it is, and whether OCR will be needed
  pdf-text  [opts] <file>          text of anything: PDF (OCR when scanned),
                                   .docx .xlsx .xlsm .xls .doc .odt .rtf
      --ocr=auto|never|force       default auto: OCR only for a scan
      --lang=ces+eng               OCR languages
  pdf-tables <file>                tables as TSV (Office formats only)
  pdf-pages [opts] <file.pdf>      render pages to PNG for visual reading
      --pages=N-M --dpi=150 --out=DIR

Documents are read from /work, which is the mounted directory.
Underlying tools stay available too: pdftotext, pdftoppm, pdfinfo, pdfimages,
ocrmypdf, tesseract, qpdf, gs, antiword, catdoc, odt2txt, unrtf.
EOF
